  "question": {
    "text": "Three blocks are arranged on a horizontal table&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCD</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. The strings and pulleys are massless and both the pulleys stand vertical. The strings connecting blocks <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are also vertical and are perpendicular to faces&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math> which are mutually perpendicular to each other. If <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> respectively. Coefficient of friction between the block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp; and the surface is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></math> then, frictional force on <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0151_8636c40c698b.jpg\" />"
  },
